    {
      "id": "workspace-toolbar-instructions",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Route Authoring Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": 831,
        "y": -376
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 260,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "workspace-toolbar-declaration"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# The audit, in twelve findings\n\n**Wrong**\n1. The Tidy tooltip says it moves graphs placed by hand; the code keeps them.\n2. The zoom percentage is a button with no click handler.\n3. The bar zooms to 400%; the workspace caps at 300%.\n4. \"Save workspace\" is the main Save with the workspace focused, beside \"Save all\" and \"Save selection as graph\".\n\n**Unclear**\n5. The bar and the right-click menu name and list commands differently.\n6. Disabled commands give no reason.\n7. \"Fit graph\" and \"Fit workspace\" are easy to confuse, and nothing shows which is in force.\n8. Long text labels, no icons: the bar is wide.\n\n**Layout and access**\n9. At 600px it wraps to four rows over the canvas, with no overflow menu.\n10. It has role=\"toolbar\" but 15 tab stops, not one with arrow keys.\n11. Colours are written into the component, not taken from the theme.\n12. No shortcuts are shown.\n\n**Coverage:** none in npm test; only a browser smoke script. **Safety is fine:** Clear workspace asks before discarding unsaved changes.\n\n# The order\n\nPhase 1 and the disabled reasons first: they are small and they are most of the value. Then the tests, then the shared list, then the narrow layout and the keyboard. The names of the saves wait for your word."
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792258325446,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
